<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB unit gets electrical orders.</title>
<headline>ABB unit gets electrical orders.</headline>
<dateline>BADEN, Switzerland 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABB Industrie AG, a unit of electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG, said it had won orders worth 65 million Swiss francs for electrical equipment for cement plants in Egypt and Indonesia.</p>
<p>It said two orders, each worth 23 million francs, were for complete electrical installations for the expansion of the Suez Cement Company plant and for another plant owned by the Egyptian Cement Company.</p>
<p>In Indonesia, it said P.T. Indocement Tunggal Prakarsa near Jakarta had ordered a full electrical installation with automation for a new production line. This order was part of a consortium and was worth 19 million francs, ABB Industrie said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
